---
title: "Shared Bibliography"
description: "A page citing the project-wide `.bib` without declaring one of its own."
---

## Citing without declaring

This page has no `bibliography:` in its front matter. It cites
[@shannon1948] anyway, because `_site.yml` declares the project-wide
`bibliography: references.bib` that every page of the site inherits.

That is the whole point of the key: a series of posts sharing one reference file
declares it once, instead of retyping the same line in every front matter and
letting the copies drift.
